        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Makers: Women Who Make America\n- People: Oprah Winfrey, Hillary Clinton, Ellen DeGeneres\n- Topics: women from different social strata, media recognition, wealth, philanthropy\n\nFacts:\n- Makers: Women Who Make America features interviews with women from many social strata, including politicians such as Hillary Clinton, television stars such as Ellen DeGeneres and Oprah Winfrey, and workers such as flight attendants, coal miners, and phone company workers.\n- Oprah Winfrey was born as Orpah Gail Winfrey on January 29, 1954.\n- Oprah Winfrey is an American media proprietor, talk show host, actress, producer, and philanthropist.\n- Oprah Winfrey has been dubbed the \"Queen of All Media.\"\n- Oprah Winfrey has been ranked the richest African-American, the greatest black philanthropist in American history, and North America's first black multi-billionaire.",
